#: ../../source/llm-wiki_SKILL.md:236
msgid "Core Operations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/llm-wiki_SKILL.md:238
msgid "1. Ingest"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/llm-wiki_SKILL.md:240
msgid ""
"When the user provides a source (URL, file, paste), integrate it into the"
" wiki:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/llm-wiki_SKILL.md:242
msgid "① **Capture the raw source:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/llm-wiki_SKILL.md:243
msgid "URL → use `web_extract` to get markdown, save to `raw/articles/`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/llm-wiki_SKILL.md:244
msgid "PDF → use `web_extract` (handles PDFs), save to `raw/papers/`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/llm-wiki_SKILL.md:245
msgid "Pasted text → save to appropriate `raw/` subdirectory"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/llm-wiki_SKILL.md:246
msgid "Name the file descriptively: `raw/articles/karpathy-llm-wiki-2026.md`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/llm-wiki_SKILL.md:248
msgid ""
"② **Discuss takeaways** with the user — what's interesting, what matters "
"for    the domain. (Skip this in automated/cron contexts — proceed "
"directly.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/llm-wiki_SKILL.md:251
msgid ""
"③ **Check what already exists** — search index.md and use `search_files` "
"to find    existing pages for mentioned entities/concepts. This is the "
"difference between    a growing wiki and a pile of duplicates."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/llm-wiki_SKILL.md:255
msgid "④ **Write or update wiki pages:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/llm-wiki_SKILL.md:256
msgid ""
"**New entities/concepts:** Create pages only if they meet the Page "
"Thresholds in SCHEMA.md (2+ source mentions, or central to one source)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/llm-wiki_SKILL.md:258
msgid ""
"**Existing pages:** Add new information, update facts, bump `updated` "
"date. When new info contradicts existing content, follow the Update "
"Policy."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/llm-wiki_SKILL.md:260
msgid ""
"**Cross-reference:** Every new or updated page must link to at least 2 "
"other pages via `[[wikilinks]]`. Check that existing pages link back."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/llm-wiki_SKILL.md:262
msgid "**Tags:** Only use tags from the taxonomy in SCHEMA.md"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/llm-wiki_SKILL.md:264
msgid "⑤ **Update navigation:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/llm-wiki_SKILL.md:265
msgid "Add new pages to `index.md` under the correct section, alphabetically"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/llm-wiki_SKILL.md:266
msgid "Update the \"Total pages\" count and \"Last updated\" date in index header"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/llm-wiki_SKILL.md:267
msgid "Append to `log.md`: `## [YYYY-MM-DD] ingest | Source Title`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/llm-wiki_SKILL.md:268
msgid "List every file created or updated in the log entry"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/llm-wiki_SKILL.md:270
msgid ""
"⑥ **Report what changed** — list every file created or updated to the "
"user."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/llm-wiki_SKILL.md:272
msgid ""
"A single source can trigger updates across 5-15 wiki pages. This is "
"normal and desired — it's the compounding effect."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/llm-wiki_SKILL.md:275
msgid "2. Query"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/llm-wiki_SKILL.md:277
msgid "When the user asks a question about the wiki's domain:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/llm-wiki_SKILL.md:279
msgid ""
"① **Read `index.md`** to identify relevant pages. ② **For wikis with 100+"
" pages**, also `search_files` across all `.md` files    for key terms — "
"the index alone may miss relevant content. ③ **Read the relevant pages** "
"using `read_file`. ④ **Synthesize an answer** from the compiled "
"knowledge. Cite the wiki pages    you drew from: \"Based on [[page-a]] "
"and [[page-b]]...\" ⑤ **File valuable answers back** — if the answer is a"
" substantial comparison,    deep dive, or novel synthesis, create a page "
"in `queries/` or `comparisons/`.    Don't file trivial lookups — only "
"answers that would be painful to re-derive. ⑥ **Update log.md** with the "
"query and whether it was filed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/llm-wiki_SKILL.md:290
msgid "3. Lint"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/llm-wiki_SKILL.md:292
msgid "When the user asks to lint, health-check, or audit the wiki:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/llm-wiki_SKILL.md:294
msgid ""
"① **Orphan pages:** Find pages with no inbound `[[wikilinks]]` from other"
" pages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/llm-wiki_SKILL.md:305
msgid ""
"② **Broken wikilinks:** Find `[[links]]` that point to pages that don't "
"exist."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/llm-wiki_SKILL.md:307
msgid ""
"③ **Index completeness:** Every wiki page should appear in `index.md`. "
"Compare    the filesystem against index entries."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/llm-wiki_SKILL.md:310
msgid ""
"④ **Frontmatter validation:** Every wiki page must have all required "
"fields    (title, created, updated, type, tags, sources). Tags must be in"
" the taxonomy."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/llm-wiki_SKILL.md:313
msgid ""
"⑤ **Stale content:** Pages whose `updated` date is >90 days older than "
"the most    recent source that mentions the same entities."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/llm-wiki_SKILL.md:316
msgid ""
"⑥ **Contradictions:** Pages on the same topic with conflicting claims. "
"Look for    pages that share tags/entities but state different facts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/llm-wiki_SKILL.md:319
msgid "⑦ **Page size:** Flag pages over 200 lines — candidates for splitting."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/llm-wiki_SKILL.md:321
msgid ""
"⑧ **Tag audit:** List all tags in use, flag any not in the SCHEMA.md "
"taxonomy."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/llm-wiki_SKILL.md:323
msgid "⑨ **Log rotation:** If log.md exceeds 500 entries, rotate it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/llm-wiki_SKILL.md:325
msgid ""
"⑩ **Report findings** with specific file paths and suggested actions, "
"grouped by    severity (broken links > orphans > stale content > style "
"issues)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/llm-wiki_SKILL.md:328
msgid "⑪ **Append to log.md:** `## [YYYY-MM-DD] lint | N issues found`"
msgstr ""

